## Purpose
- Define where backend changes belong and how to keep them safe.

## Source of truth
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Program.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Configuration/*.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Controllers/AuthController*.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Data/AuthDbContext.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth.Tests/Controllers/*.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth.Tests/Services/*.cs`

## Do
- Add API logic in auth service controllers/services, not in gateway.
- Keep DI in `Configuration/ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs`.
- Keep pipeline/middleware changes in `Configuration/WebApplicationExtensions.cs`.
- Register new data model changes in `AuthDbContext` and migrations.
- Add/adjust tests next to touched behavior (controller/service tests).

## Don't
- Do not hardcode secrets in `appsettings*.json`; use Aspire AppHost JWT for local dev, root `.env.staging` for Compose staging, or optional service `.env.example` templates.
- Do not add endpoints outside `/api/auth` unless explicitly changing route contract.
- Do not skip validation for request DTOs.

## Checklist
- Endpoint compiles, mapped by controller attributes, covered by tests.
- Config keys are bound through options/`IConfiguration`, not magic strings in handlers.
- Logging level/shape remains consistent with Serilog setup.
